research-service-setup — dual-use content disclosure

What this package is

research-service-setup is a one-time setup helper for the research service
used by the "research3" agent skill (https://github.com/random-react-dev/research-setup).
It installs the research service's local component on a Mac so the skill can
run its headless research jobs in the background.

What it does that can look like malware to an automated scanner

- The bin (bin/setup.js) downloads a Python setup script over HTTPS from the
  research service's server (https://ask-gateway.r95426882.workers.dev/api/research/setup)
  and executes it with a local Python 3 interpreter.
- That script, in turn, downloads a signature-verified release archive from the
  same server, installs it under ~/Library/Application Support/ResearchRunner,
  and registers a macOS launchd LaunchAgent so the installed service component
  keeps running.
- It stores a per-device identifier file (device.json) under the same
  ~/Library/Application Support/ResearchRunner directory.

In short: it downloads and executes code and installs a persistent local
service — the same pattern as many legitimate installer CLIs.

What it sends over the network

- Requests to https://ask-gateway.r95426882.workers.dev only: fetching the
  setup script, downloading the signed release archive, and readiness checks
  that carry the device identifier. No other destinations, no telemetry.

Intended legitimate use

The owner of the Mac runs this once (directly or through their coding agent)
to set up the research service that their installed skill depends on. Reruns
are no-ops when the service is already installed and verified. The public
source code is at https://github.com/random-react-dev/research-setup.
